# StatChip — one number and its label, on one line, sized to sit beside two or
# three others: "1.2M Followers", "348 views", "12.4K members". Extracted from
# `profile/ProfileHeader`'s own follow-count row, which drew this shape once and
# hard-coded it, the way this library's stat rows keep starting.
#
#     use StatChipRow():
#         use StatChip(followers, "Followers")
#         use StatChip(following, "Following")
#
# ── WHY THIS IS NOT `data/Stat` ──────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# `data/Stat` is a dashboard's own headline figure: big type, its own column, a
# delta arrow underneath. A chip is not the reason the reader opened the page —
# it is one fact among several, inline, in a header or a tile, and it is scanned
# rather than read. Different object, not a smaller size of the same one.
#
# ── `compact`, NOT `commas` ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# `data/Stat` takes its value as pre-formatted text because a dashboard number
# wants the exact figure (`commas`, a currency, a duration) and the host is the
# only place that knows which. A chip wants the OPPOSITE: "240.1M Followers", not
# "240,133,982 Followers", because a chip is read at a glance and a glance wants
# the rounded form. So `StatChip` takes the raw `int` and calls `compact` itself,
# which is also why it is `int` and not `text` — there is nothing for the host to
# format. `StatChipText` is here for the one case that still needs the host's own
# words: a stat that already arrived as a string ("Top 1%", a currency amount).
app FacetUI:
    css:
        [data-fa-mount] .x-statchips { display: flex; flex-direction: row; flex-wrap: wrap;
                       align-items: baseline; gap: 16px; border: none; background: none; padding: 0; }
        [data-fa-mount] .x-statchip { display: inline-flex; align-items: baseline; gap: 4px;
                      font-size: 14px; color: var(--fa-muted); border: none; background: none; padding: 0; }
        [data-fa-mount] .x-statchip-n { color: var(--fa-fg); font-weight: 700;
                        font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }
    component StatChipRow():
        row class "x-statchips":
            slot
    component StatChip(value: int, label: text):
        row class "x-statchip":
            text "{compact(value)}" class "x-statchip-n"
            text "{label}"
    component StatChipText(value: text, label: text):
        row class "x-statchip":
            text "{value}" class "x-statchip-n"
            text "{label}"
